  "verdict": "gain",
  "measurement_reason": "F14 has measured native argument-normalization gains with no confirmed loss. One ordinary path costs 0.05258 -> 0.03102 us (-40.99%) for a short path and 0.05105 -> 0.03348 us (-34.41%) for a long path. 64 ordinary paths improve 87.25-87.55%; 512 short paths improve 12.78056 -> 1.33663 us (-89.54%) and long paths improve 89.44%. Raw allocations fall 70.004 -> 6.001 per 64-path call and 521.037 -> 9.003 per 512-path call, removing one temporary per ordinary argument. No-path control time is neutral (-0.62%) and allocations remain 2.000. All candidate observations retain exact leading/trailing/whitespace-only paths and order. These changed-output cases are diagnostic; their speed differences are not used as same-work performance gains.",
